// What is hidden on a tile until someone searches for it (old DiscoveryGenerator, DiscoveryFeatureFactory,
// FeatureFactory harvestables, salvage and EnvironmentalDetailFactory). Generated per tile from the
// seed, never saved. Loaded once by Content; ContentTests checks every name in here resolves.
//
// finds: what a discovery makes, by id. Either a stock (work Harvest or Salvage, minutes per cycle,
//   items) or a natural shelter (shelter: its kind; a level with a spread is level + up to spread;
//   a cap left out is the kind's, and a find's caps are at least its own levels).
// details: quick finds (work Detail), by the old detail ids.
// found: what the finder reads on finding it, one line of these picked for each place it lies
//   (the old ForageStrategy discovery messages).
// An item, rolled in order: chance (default 1), then units [units, unitsMax], then each unit's kg in
//   [kgPerUnit, kgPerUnitMax] when that is given. A harvest gives units of kgPerUnit, one a cycle,
//   regrowing one per respawnHoursPerUnit (stated on every harvest item; 0 never). Salvage and details give everything at once, all
//   the units' kilos together. anyOf: one of these, drawn after every item's counts. gear: a gear kind
//   (items.json), whole. shuffle: these items shuffled, then take [take, takeMax] of them, each rolled.
//   Every anyOf of a find is one draw: the find is one wood, so its lists name their woods in one order.
//   requiresTool: only someone carrying that tool works the item (a wood find's firewood needs an axe);
//   the rest come by hand. Wood in a wood find never regrows.
//
// terrains, cave: the draws, in order. Each entry is there on its spawnChance and found after about
//   expectedHours of searching. An entry that waitsFor a system not built yet (small game, events)
//   still takes its turn, so the draw is the old one, and leaves nothing.
// detailDraws: the details each terrain can have (a name twice is twice as likely); examineOnly are
//   the ones with nothing to take, which only ever told a story and leave nothing.
